Yet Another Embarrassingly Stupid Death

So I've been playing NetHack for about a year now, but I'm still a
total newbie, as the following anecdote proves:

Yesterday I started Kiryn III-Val-Hum-Fem-Law. As is usual with these
things, she had potential. Found an altar early on (neutral,
unfortunately) which I used to buc identify my inventory. Also found a
wand of lightning, which I id'ed by engraving. Killed a bunch of
floating eyes and got ESP (nearly got YASD'ed though when I blundered
into one). Killed a bunch of other stuff, too, and got up to XL 8. My
one misfortune (newbie mistake, more like) was Felix the kitten's
early passing. Got hungry, so I threw an egg at him. Hey, it works
with tripe rations, right? Splat! You kill poor Felix! You hear the
rumble of distant thunder... I wasn't doing too well armor wise until
the mines, where I got iron shoes, dwarvish helm, and dwarvish
mithril-coat. I was getting plenty of other stuff, too, and became
stressed (I know, big newbie mistake). So I figured I'd head down to
minetown and id it on the altar. So I get to minetown, and a soldier
ant greets me. I hate the buggers, so I zap him with my wand of
lightning (wasn't in the best of health at the time, didn't want to
risk it). Killed the ant, but the bolt continued on to miss a
watchman, who got angry. He chucks a spear at me, and another soldier
ant appears. Taking it turn by turn now, I vaporize both of them with
the wand. Now I have to deal with a gnome lord who has been a
secondary concern until now. I take a swing, he hits, and I'm down to
8/72 hp. This is where I commit the inevitable culmination of my prior
stupid mistakes. My options included 1)Take another swing and hope
it's enough to kill him, 2)Zap him with the wand and hope it misses me
on the rebound, and 3)Quaff one of my three potions and hope it's
healing. Granted, they were all somewhat chancy, but a lot better than
4)Pray to Tyr, even after killing my pet and a watchman. So of course
I chose option 4. You begin praying to Tyr. The gnome lord hits! You
die... DYWYPI? I was especially bummed because my inventory turned out
to contain a potion of full healing... and that mithril coat had a +3
enchantment on it. There were also a lot of nice jewels.

The moral of the story? Actually, there are more than one. 1)Don't
throw eggs at your pet, 2)Always check to make sure a wand blast won't
have undesirable consequences, and 3)Tyr doesn't always answer your
prayers.

